# Security Rules - Metadata-Driven Platform

## Core Security Framework

- **Authentication**: JWT with refresh tokens, 2FA for admin accounts
- **Authorization**: Metadata-driven RBAC with fine-grained permissions
- **Encryption**: AES-256 for data at rest, TLS 1.3 for data in transit
- **Metadata Security**: Secure access to platform metadata and component catalog
- **Tenant Isolation**: Complete security boundaries between tenants
- **Component Security**: Secure component installation and execution

## Authentication Standards (MANDATORY)

- **JWT Tokens**: 15-minute access tokens, 7-day refresh tokens with tenant context
- **Multi-Factor**: 2FA required for admin and financial roles
- **Password Security**: Bcrypt hashing, never plain text storage
- **Magic Links**: Secure passwordless authentication with time limits
- **Tenant Context**: MANDATORY tenant_id in all authentication tokens

## Metadata Security (MANDATORY)

- **Component Catalog**: Secure access to ComponentDefinitions and module manifests
- **Entity Metadata**: Permission-based access to EntityDefinitions and FieldDefinitions
- **Layout Security**: Restrict layout and form definitions by user roles
- **Workflow Security**: Secure workflow definition access and execution
- **Marketplace Security**: Validate component sources and signatures

- **Permission Patterns**: Use structured permission naming for metadata access
- **Dynamic Permissions**: Generate permissions from entity and component definitions
- **Access Validation**: Always check permissions before metadata operations

## Authorization & Access Control (MANDATORY)

- **RBAC Model**: Metadata-driven role and permission system
- **Dynamic Permissions**: Permissions generated from EntityDefinitions
- **Component Permissions**: Fine-grained access to platform components
- **Workflow Permissions**: Secure workflow trigger and action permissions
- **Field-Level Security**: Hide/protect fields based on metadata permissions

## Multi-Tenant Security (MANDATORY)

- **Complete Isolation**: Absolute separation of tenant data and metadata
- **Database Security**: Row-level security for tenant boundaries
- **Component Isolation**: Tenant-specific component installations
- **Metadata Boundaries**: Prevent cross-tenant metadata access
- **Workflow Isolation**: Secure tenant-specific workflow execution

## Component & Module Security (MANDATORY)

- **Code Signing**: Verify component authenticity and integrity
- **Sandbox Execution**: Isolate component execution environments
- **Permission Declaration**: Components must declare required permissions
- **Dependency Validation**: Secure dependency resolution and validation
- **Marketplace Vetting**: Security review for marketplace components

- **Multi-Layer Validation**: Signature, permissions, and vulnerability scanning
- **Component Integrity**: Verify component authenticity before installation
- **Security Scanning**: Automated security checks for all marketplace components

## Data Protection & Encryption (MANDATORY)

- **Sensitive Metadata**: Encrypt component code and configuration
- **Field-Level Encryption**: Encrypt sensitive field values
- **Key Management**: Environment-based encryption keys, never hardcoded
- **Transport Security**: TLS 1.3 for all API communications
- **Backup Encryption**: Encrypt all database backups and metadata exports

## Workflow Security (MANDATORY)

- **Trigger Validation**: Secure workflow trigger conditions
- **Action Permissions**: Validate permissions for workflow actions
- **Execution Isolation**: Isolate workflow execution per tenant
- **External Integration**: Secure external API calls from workflows
- **Audit Trail**: Complete logging of workflow security events

## Platform API Security (MANDATORY)

- **Metadata API Protection**: Rate limiting and access control for metadata APIs
- **Component Catalog Security**: Secure component discovery and installation
- **Dynamic CRUD Security**: Permission validation for generated endpoints
- **Webhook Security**: Secure webhook endpoints with signature validation
- **Integration Security**: Secure external system integrations

## Marketplace Security (MANDATORY)

- **Creator Verification**: Identity verification for component creators
- **Component Review**: Security review process for marketplace submissions
- **Licensing Validation**: Secure license checking and enforcement
- **Revenue Security**: Secure payment processing for component sales
- **Vulnerability Management**: Continuous security monitoring of components

## Input Validation & Sanitization (MANDATORY)

- **Metadata Validation**: Strict validation of all metadata inputs
- **Component Props**: Validate component props against JSON schemas
- **Workflow Data**: Sanitize all workflow input and output data
- **Dynamic Query Protection**: Prevent injection in dynamic queries
- **Field Validation**: Validate field values against metadata rules

## Security Monitoring & Auditing (MANDATORY)

- **Metadata Access Logging**: Log all metadata access and modifications
- **Component Activity**: Monitor component installations and executions
- **Workflow Monitoring**: Track workflow execution and security events
- **Suspicious Patterns**: Detect unusual metadata or component access
- **Security Alerts**: Automated alerts for security violations

## Compliance & Privacy (MANDATORY)

- **GDPR Compliance**: Data protection for European tenants
- **SOC 2 Compliance**: Security controls for enterprise customers
- **Data Residency**: Respect tenant data location requirements
- **Right to Delete**: Secure data deletion including metadata
- **Audit Requirements**: Maintain audit trails for compliance

## Infrastructure Security (MANDATORY)

- **Container Security**: Secure component execution environments
- **Network Isolation**: VPC isolation for tenant database clusters
- **Secrets Management**: Secure storage of API keys and certificates
- **Backup Security**: Encrypted backups with secure access controls
- **Monitoring**: Security event monitoring and intrusion detection

## What NOT to Do

- ❌ Never expose metadata structure to unauthorized users
- ❌ Don't skip component signature verification
- ❌ Never allow cross-tenant metadata access
- ❌ Don't trust user-submitted component code without validation
- ❌ Never skip workflow permission validation
- ❌ Don't store sensitive data in component definitions
- ❌ Never allow direct database access bypassing metadata security
- ❌ Don't skip audit logging for security-sensitive operations
- ❌ Never ignore component dependency security
- ❌ Don't trust client-side metadata validation alone

## Platform-Specific Security

- **Metadata Integrity**: Protect platform metadata from tampering
- **Component Sandbox**: Isolate component execution environments
- **Tenant Boundaries**: Absolute security isolation between tenants
- **Marketplace Trust**: Build and maintain component marketplace trust
- **Runtime Security**: Secure dynamic code execution and metadata processing
